1
00:00:01,667 --> 00:00:03,503
"Previously on The Mentalist..."

2
00:00:11,052 --> 00:00:12,637
"I can't do this anymore."

3
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:15,139
"I can't watch you
do this work. I mean..."

4
00:00:15,681 --> 00:00:17,475
It coulda been you
in that coffin.

5
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:21,187
You can't keep pulling me from
the path of oncoming trains.

6
00:00:21,979 --> 00:00:24,357
I'm leaving.
I have to go.

7
00:00:40,456 --> 00:00:43,334
- But why Greece?
- It's the cradle of civilization.

8
00:00:43,459 --> 00:00:45,836
Well, yeah, like
3 thousand years ago.

9
00:00:45,962 --> 00:00:47,213
Uh, what have they done
for us lately?

10
00:00:47,588 --> 00:00:49,215
Okay, so, where should I go?

11
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:51,467
You...

12
00:00:52,218 --> 00:00:53,469
You should stay.

13
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:56,472
Study abroad is overrated.

14
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:05,523
What?

15
00:01:06,816 --> 00:01:10,069
- Is somebody out there?
- Don't even joke about that.

16
00:01:11,404 --> 00:01:12,613
Donnie, go!

17
00:01:34,927 --> 00:01:37,346
Please... Don't, please.

18
00:01:47,773 --> 00:01:49,567
- Morning, Lisbon.
- Cho...

19
00:01:49,817 --> 00:01:51,694
Uh, this is Park Ranger
Jill Ayres.

20
00:01:51,819 --> 00:01:53,738
Uh, she was the first person
on the crime scene.

21
00:01:54,113 --> 00:01:56,616
- Glad to have the FBI's help.
- Happy to be here.

22
00:01:57,533 --> 00:01:59,285
- Who found 'em?
- I did.

23
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:00,703
I was doing
my morning rounds.

24
00:02:00,828 --> 00:02:02,747
I saw the tire tracks
going off the side.

25
00:02:02,955 --> 00:02:04,081
Any idea what they were doin'
out here?

26
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:05,750
Well, it's a nice view,
from the top of the hill.

27
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:07,043
Kids come out here to park.

28
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:08,711
Techs found nine millimeter casings

29
00:02:08,836 --> 00:02:10,546
at the top of the hill
next to the tire tracks.

30
00:02:10,671 --> 00:02:11,964
So, the shooting took place
up there.

31
00:02:12,089 --> 00:02:13,966
They go the wrong way
and end up down here.

32
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:15,843
She try to make
a run for it?

33
00:02:15,968 --> 00:02:17,720
Uh, there are drag marks
from the car to the body

34
00:02:17,845 --> 00:02:19,305
so, the killer must have
moved her.

35
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:20,765
Maybe he was searching
for something.

36
00:02:20,931 --> 00:02:22,516
Maybe the killer tried to take
the body up the hill

37
00:02:22,642 --> 00:02:23,684
and got to that steep part...

38
00:02:23,851 --> 00:02:24,977
Realized it wasn't gonna happen.

39
00:02:25,269 --> 00:02:27,897
- But why move her at all?
- That's a good question.

40
00:02:28,022 --> 00:02:29,315
Thank you, Ranger.
We'll be in touch.

41
00:02:29,565 --> 00:02:30,608
You bet.

42
00:02:32,234 --> 00:02:33,486
The vultures are here.

43
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:37,239
Great.

44
00:02:38,032 --> 00:02:39,617
We could use
Jane's read on this.

45
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:41,118
It's been a week.
You haven't heard from him?

46
00:02:41,410 --> 00:02:43,412
No. No, not since the funeral.

47
00:02:43,579 --> 00:02:45,790
All right, well, Abbott's starting
to prep his move to DC.

48
00:02:45,998 --> 00:02:47,041
We're shorthanded.

49
00:02:47,166 --> 00:02:48,459
We need to close this
before it gets out of hand.

50
00:02:48,876 --> 00:02:50,961
Now's not the time for one
of his disappearing acts.

51
00:02:53,631 --> 00:02:54,674
You want me to call him?

52
00:02:54,799 --> 00:02:56,717
- No. Nah, I'll call him.
- Okay.

53
00:03:53,814 --> 00:03:56,525
Wylie's doing background checks
on Donnie and Megan.

54
00:03:56,650 --> 00:03:59,653
We can't seem to find any reason
somebody would want them dead.

55
00:03:59,778 --> 00:04:01,864
They seem like a couple
of nice college kids.

56
00:04:02,573 --> 00:04:05,826
Sometimes, national parks
are used by drug cultivators.

57
00:04:06,285 --> 00:04:08,579
Now, maybe these kids were at
the wrong place, at the wrong time.

58
00:04:08,787 --> 00:04:11,373
We've got a contact in the park rangers.
I can ask her to come in.

59
00:04:11,498 --> 00:04:12,791
{\an8}Anything come back
from forensics?

60
00:04:12,916 --> 00:04:15,502
{\an8}Uh, they were both killed
with the same gun: 9mm.

61
00:04:15,711 --> 00:04:17,379
{\an8}- Hm.
- No hits from ballistics.

62
00:04:18,255 --> 00:04:20,549
- Autopsy turned up somethin'.
- What?

63
00:04:20,674 --> 00:04:22,968
Both Donnie and Megan
were missing a fingernail.

64
00:04:23,594 --> 00:04:24,845
They didn't lose it
in the crash?

65
00:04:24,970 --> 00:04:26,346
The ME thinks
they were pulled out.

66
00:04:26,472 --> 00:04:28,599
{\an8}Huh, Add that to Megan's body
being moved

67
00:04:28,724 --> 00:04:31,727
{\an8}and this case is startin'
to feel pretty strange.

68
00:04:32,144 --> 00:04:33,187
Good work.

69
00:04:34,021 --> 00:04:35,689
So, no word from Jane, huh?

70
00:04:35,856 --> 00:04:37,483
Uh, he's not returning my calls.

71
00:04:38,233 --> 00:04:39,943
{\an8}I know you two are working
something out...

72
00:04:40,110 --> 00:04:41,904
{\an8}but these murders are starting
to get headline news.

73
00:04:42,029 --> 00:04:44,406
- We need Jane.
- I'm handling it.

74
00:04:45,324 --> 00:04:46,366
{\an8}Okay.

75
00:05:24,196 --> 00:05:25,322
{\an8}Afternoon, Officer.

76
00:05:25,906 --> 00:05:27,699
Sir, are you the registered
owner of this vehicle?

77
00:05:27,908 --> 00:05:30,077
- I am.
- May I see your license, please?

78
00:05:30,536 --> 00:05:31,578
Sure.

79
00:05:34,957 --> 00:05:36,834
{\an8}So, you are Patrick Jane.

80
00:05:37,167 --> 00:05:39,670
{\an8}All day, every day... Unfortunately.

81
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:42,548
- Step out of the vehicle.
- Okay.

82
00:05:44,007 --> 00:05:45,259
{\an8}- Hands up.
- All right.

83
00:05:45,384 --> 00:05:46,426
{\an8}Okay.

84
00:05:51,890 --> 00:05:52,933
{\an8}Thorough.

85
00:05:53,308 --> 00:05:55,936
{\an8}Sir, you have a warrant out
for your arrest in Austin, Texas.

86
00:05:56,436 --> 00:05:58,814
{\an8}- What's the charge?
- Failure to appear.

87
00:06:01,859 --> 00:06:03,485
{\an8}Oh, yeah, that's funny.

88
00:06:11,451 --> 00:06:13,245
- Thanks for coming in.
- Glad to.

89
00:06:13,412 --> 00:06:14,454
Have a seat.

90
00:06:14,955 --> 00:06:15,998
{\an8}Nice office.

91
00:06:16,331 --> 00:06:18,417
{\an8}I don't get a lot
of air conditioning in my life.

92
00:06:18,792 --> 00:06:20,586
Anything going down in the park
that we should know about?

93
00:06:21,378 --> 00:06:22,421
Like what?

94
00:06:22,546 --> 00:06:23,839
{\an8}Something Donnie and Megan
may have seen

95
00:06:23,964 --> 00:06:25,173
{\an8}that somebody didn't want
them to see?

96
00:06:25,299 --> 00:06:26,341
{\an8}Maybe a drug operation?

97
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,886
{\an8}Uh, we did a major sweep
of the park a few months ago

98
00:06:29,011 --> 00:06:30,053
{\an8}cleaned it out.

99
00:06:32,639 --> 00:06:33,682
Poachers.

100
00:06:34,016 --> 00:06:35,809
We've been finding deer
in the forest

101
00:06:35,934 --> 00:06:37,519
just the backstrap cut out.

102
00:06:37,644 --> 00:06:38,729
Any idea who's behind it?

103
00:06:38,979 --> 00:06:40,814
The best bet's a couple of fellows
with a shack

104
00:06:40,939 --> 00:06:43,400
just outside the park.
The Whitmer brothers.

105
00:06:43,525 --> 00:06:45,986
Marcus Whitmer's on probation
for aggravated assault.

106
00:06:59,499 --> 00:07:00,542
Hey.

107
00:07:02,461 --> 00:07:03,795
Yeah, looks fresh.

108
00:07:07,966 --> 00:07:09,009
Hey.

109
00:07:09,968 --> 00:07:12,554
- The hell is this?
- FBI. Put the knife down, sir.

110
00:07:18,602 --> 00:07:20,103
Put the gun on the ground.
Do it now.

111
00:07:20,228 --> 00:07:21,355
It's all right.

112
00:07:22,856 --> 00:07:24,149
Do what he says, Marcus.

113
00:07:24,983 --> 00:07:26,026
Do it now!

114
00:07:31,448 --> 00:07:32,491
Hey!

115
00:07:33,075 --> 00:07:34,117
Turn over!

116
00:07:34,826 --> 00:07:35,953
- Come on!
- Agent Cho!

117
00:07:36,078 --> 00:07:37,120
Cuff him!

118
00:07:37,704 --> 00:07:39,790
I didn't know you were law.
I wasn't gonna shoot you.

119
00:07:41,083 --> 00:07:42,751
Damn near busted my ribs.

120
00:07:46,296 --> 00:07:47,339
Get up.

121
00:07:50,550 --> 00:07:52,177
You know if Donnie and Megan
were planning to meet

122
00:07:52,302 --> 00:07:53,887
with anyone
when they left the dorm?

123
00:07:56,431 --> 00:07:58,308
Of course... Just something
we have to ask.

124
00:08:00,268 --> 00:08:02,145
Uh, well, if you think of anything
or hear anything

125
00:08:02,312 --> 00:08:03,480
please, give us a call.

126
00:08:04,481 --> 00:08:05,524
Thank you.

127
00:08:07,359 --> 00:08:09,319
Excuse me... Hi.

128
00:08:09,653 --> 00:08:11,363
- Can I help you?
- My name's Ree Osbourne.

129
00:08:11,488 --> 00:08:13,365
I'm here about the two
that were shot last night

130
00:08:13,490 --> 00:08:14,700
The two in the forest.

131
00:08:14,825 --> 00:08:16,410
Do you have information
about the case?

132
00:08:16,535 --> 00:08:18,578
No, I don't.
My brother does.

133
00:08:19,788 --> 00:08:22,582
- That's your brother?
- Yeah. Gabriel.

134
00:08:24,042 --> 00:08:25,293
I'm Agent Wylie.

135
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:28,797
What do you know
about the murders?

136
00:08:31,758 --> 00:08:33,802
He's shy.
I had to drag him over here.

137
00:08:33,927 --> 00:08:34,970
He doesn't like talking

138
00:08:35,095 --> 00:08:37,514
but I told him he had to say
what he saw.

139
00:08:38,265 --> 00:08:39,474
He witnessed the crime?

140
00:08:40,267 --> 00:08:42,060
No, he didn't witness it.
He saw it.

141
00:08:42,269 --> 00:08:43,311
In his head?

142
00:08:43,979 --> 00:08:46,982
- You mean, he's a psychic?
- Yeah... Psychic.

143
00:08:47,357 --> 00:08:48,400
Gabriel.

144
00:08:49,609 --> 00:08:52,529
Come over here.
Tell this man what you have to say.

145
00:08:52,696 --> 00:08:53,739
He's loud.

146
00:08:55,198 --> 00:08:56,241
I'm loud?

147
00:08:59,202 --> 00:09:01,496
The crying is loud.

148
00:09:02,873 --> 00:09:04,624
I hear you crying, inside.

149
00:09:05,834 --> 00:09:08,754
- What are you talking about?
- I'm so sorry.

150
00:09:12,299 --> 00:09:15,135
See, I don't think
my brother's a psychic.

151
00:09:15,719 --> 00:09:17,429
I know he's a psychic.

152
00:09:23,685 --> 00:09:24,936
Can you please
come with me?

153
00:09:26,313 --> 00:09:28,356
The poachers were out
hunting wild boar

154
00:09:28,482 --> 00:09:29,941
12 hours away, last night.

155
00:09:30,192 --> 00:09:32,027
There's a liquor store clerk
three counties over

156
00:09:32,152 --> 00:09:33,487
that confirms their story.

157
00:09:33,653 --> 00:09:35,655
They got back
just before Cho arrived.

158
00:09:35,781 --> 00:09:38,742
Hm. Well, we're not gettin' anything
from friends or family either.

159
00:09:39,409 --> 00:09:40,786
They sound like
regular college kids.

160
00:09:40,911 --> 00:09:42,704
We've got the UT campus covered.

161
00:09:42,829 --> 00:09:45,332
We talked to friends,
classmates, professors.

162
00:09:46,917 --> 00:09:49,544
Come in.
You got somethin'?

163
00:09:50,253 --> 00:09:52,672
I have a guy who's saying
things about the murders.

164
00:09:53,215 --> 00:09:54,591
Well, what is he saying, Wylie?

165
00:09:54,883 --> 00:09:56,468
- He's a psychic.
- Ah, come on.

166
00:09:57,052 --> 00:09:59,846
I, I don't know how to explain it...
You need to talk to him.

167
00:10:08,772 --> 00:10:12,192
- You're leaving.
- Excuse me?

168
00:10:12,901 --> 00:10:14,736
You're moving on.
You're going to a new place.

169
00:10:14,986 --> 00:10:18,073
- Yeah.
- Eager to go.

170
00:10:21,368 --> 00:10:23,370
You have doubts inside
you haven't told anybody.

171
00:10:23,578 --> 00:10:24,830
Everybody has doubt

172
00:10:24,955 --> 00:10:26,873
when they're going through
a change in their life.

173
00:10:27,582 --> 00:10:29,167
Tell us what you know
about the murders of

174
00:10:29,292 --> 00:10:31,962
Donald Putnam
and Megan Brooks.

175
00:10:32,838 --> 00:10:35,215
The killer, he wanted
to take them with him.

176
00:10:36,633 --> 00:10:39,594
He wanted them.
But he couldn't.

177
00:10:42,264 --> 00:10:43,974
Took a piece of them, instead.

178
00:10:47,352 --> 00:10:48,562
Fingertips.

179
00:10:51,439 --> 00:10:53,108
So... I didn't say
that would be helpful.

180
00:10:53,358 --> 00:10:54,609
I only said it would be true.

181
00:10:56,444 --> 00:10:57,737
How do you know
about this?

182
00:10:58,864 --> 00:11:01,116
Six months ago,
I spoke to a man.

183
00:11:04,077 --> 00:11:07,664
He had so much wrongness in him,
I could hardly look at him.

184
00:11:09,749 --> 00:11:11,334
It was like starin' at the sun.

185
00:11:13,086 --> 00:11:15,922
I been waiting ever since
for somethin' like this

186
00:11:16,590 --> 00:11:18,341
- to happen.
- Who was he?

187
00:11:18,466 --> 00:11:19,759
I don't know.

188
00:11:21,011 --> 00:11:23,722
Okay. What did he look like?

189
00:11:24,472 --> 00:11:25,640
He was a man.

190
00:11:27,475 --> 00:11:28,518
He was white.

191
00:11:30,854 --> 00:11:32,731
Sorry, I'm not good with faces.

192
00:11:34,733 --> 00:11:36,109
I only see what's inside.

193
00:11:43,241 --> 00:11:44,576
So, he met the killer

194
00:11:44,701 --> 00:11:46,953
but he can't remember
a single detail about him.

195
00:11:47,078 --> 00:11:48,288
I agree.
That's suspicious.

196
00:11:48,413 --> 00:11:49,789
But he knew about the bodies
being moved

197
00:11:49,915 --> 00:11:51,124
and he knew
about the fingernails.

198
00:11:51,249 --> 00:11:52,292
Which we already knew.

199
00:11:52,417 --> 00:11:54,085
But none of those details
have been made public.

200
00:11:54,211 --> 00:11:56,004
Oh, maybe he's friends
with the crime tech...

201
00:11:56,129 --> 00:11:57,339
Or maybe he's the killer.

202
00:11:57,631 --> 00:11:58,882
And he just marched in here

203
00:11:59,007 --> 00:12:00,425
and dangled himself
right in front of us?

204
00:12:00,550 --> 00:12:03,637
It's more likely than him being
an actual honest-to-god psychic.

205
00:12:04,262 --> 00:12:05,305
What makes you so sure?

206
00:12:06,723 --> 00:12:08,350
Years of experience.

207
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:22,489
What were you doin'
in Arizona?

208
00:12:26,451 --> 00:12:29,204
- I went to the Grand Canyon.
- The Grand Canyon.

209
00:12:29,329 --> 00:12:30,372
Mm.

210
00:12:31,957 --> 00:12:34,501
- Have you been?
- No. Nah, I hear it's big.

211
00:12:34,626 --> 00:12:36,044
Huge, yeah.

212
00:12:37,254 --> 00:12:38,296
How's the tea?

213
00:12:39,839 --> 00:12:41,841
Hot. Good. Thank you.

214
00:12:42,175 --> 00:12:45,512
I woulda mailed you your cup
but I didn't know where you were.

215
00:12:46,304 --> 00:12:47,430
Well, you knew I'd be back.

216
00:12:47,555 --> 00:12:50,225
No, I didn't.
I can't read minds.

217
00:12:50,684 --> 00:12:53,853
The first time I called you,
I thought, "he missed my call".

218
00:12:54,646 --> 00:12:56,564
Second time, I thought,
"He's busy."

219
00:12:56,690 --> 00:12:58,817
"Okay, he'll call me back"

220
00:12:59,609 --> 00:13:01,653
The third time,
I thought, "He's dead."

221
00:13:01,861 --> 00:13:04,364
"He is dead in a ditch,
on the side of the road"

222
00:13:06,408 --> 00:13:07,742
I didn't mean to scare you.

223
00:13:08,034 --> 00:13:09,661
- Well, you did scare me.
- I'm sorry.

224
00:13:10,829 --> 00:13:11,871
Okay.

225
00:13:14,708 --> 00:13:17,460
I'm working through something
and I just need space to think.

226
00:13:17,585 --> 00:13:20,422
I can't soldier on,
like you, Lisbon.

227
00:13:20,839 --> 00:13:22,090
We're all upset.

228
00:13:23,216 --> 00:13:25,176
I can't just run away
from my work here.

229
00:13:25,302 --> 00:13:27,345
This job is too important to me.

230
00:13:27,679 --> 00:13:28,972
Yeah, I understand.

231
00:13:33,435 --> 00:13:36,563
What can I do for you to help you
figure things out?

232
00:13:37,314 --> 00:13:40,108
- Just tell me.
- Time. I just need some time.

233
00:13:41,359 --> 00:13:42,402
Okay.

234
00:13:42,819 --> 00:13:44,571
Time's good.
I can give you time.

235
00:13:45,613 --> 00:13:47,866
- I just need one thing from you.
- What's that?

236
00:13:48,158 --> 00:13:51,995
- Don't ignore my phone calls.
- Okay. Well, that's. That's fair.

237
00:13:53,997 --> 00:13:55,040
All right.

238
00:14:21,155 --> 00:14:24,283
Ah, Jane, welcome back.

239
00:14:24,617 --> 00:14:26,702
Not back, just stopping by.

240
00:14:26,827 --> 00:14:27,953
Oh, yeah, I figured.

241
00:14:28,496 --> 00:14:29,705
Hey, do you have a minute?

242
00:14:29,830 --> 00:14:32,416
I was wondering if you would take
a look at someone that just left.

243
00:14:32,541 --> 00:14:33,751
Abbott, I'm, I'm...

244
00:14:33,959 --> 00:14:36,671
Jane, you would find him
very interesting.

245
00:14:47,807 --> 00:14:50,726
Gabriel, could I have a moment
of your time?

246
00:14:50,935 --> 00:14:52,103
Patrick Jane.
I'm with the FBI.

247
00:14:52,228 --> 00:14:53,354
I just want to ask you
a few questions.

248
00:14:53,521 --> 00:14:54,563
You're an FBI agent?

249
00:14:55,189 --> 00:14:57,108
- He is not.
- He's right.

250
00:14:58,067 --> 00:15:01,237
You, you knew that
because you're a psychic?

251
00:15:02,279 --> 00:15:03,781
I knew that
because I'm not stupid.

252
00:15:04,865 --> 00:15:07,326
You knew that because of the way
I dress, my posture

253
00:15:07,451 --> 00:15:09,995
the way I cut my hair...
Any number of things.

254
00:15:11,539 --> 00:15:12,790
What do you want from me?

255
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:14,291
Well, I'm a student of the form.

256
00:15:14,417 --> 00:15:16,419
Just wanted
to shake your hand.

257
00:15:17,670 --> 00:15:18,921
Think I'm a fraud?

258
00:15:19,296 --> 00:15:22,341
I don't think you're a fraud.
You are a fraud.

259
00:15:24,093 --> 00:15:26,303
Might just be looking at
your reflection in a mirror.

260
00:15:26,429 --> 00:15:28,097
Then make a prediction for me.

261
00:15:28,264 --> 00:15:30,349
- So you can mock it?
- Maybe.

262
00:15:31,809 --> 00:15:33,436
There's a thing inside you.

263
00:15:34,729 --> 00:15:35,855
It's eating you.

264
00:15:37,565 --> 00:15:39,942
A thing that's lingered
in your mind for many years.

265
00:15:40,276 --> 00:15:41,736
That's called
the human condition.

266
00:15:42,778 --> 00:15:44,822
- You'll be cured.
- Wonderful.

267
00:15:46,157 --> 00:15:47,575
Cure will come
with the number three.

268
00:15:47,783 --> 00:15:51,078
"The number three"...
Huh. That's it?

269
00:15:51,954 --> 00:15:53,706
I could embellish it.
That'd be a lie.

270
00:15:55,499 --> 00:15:58,002
Number three.
You'll know it when you see it.

271
00:15:59,170 --> 00:16:00,379
Thanks for your time.

272
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:05,885
So, what do you think?

273
00:16:06,427 --> 00:16:09,013
Well, he's obviously not
a real psychic

274
00:16:09,388 --> 00:16:10,556
but he knows what he's doing.

275
00:16:10,681 --> 00:16:12,516
He's very smart, very controlled.

276
00:16:13,392 --> 00:16:15,436
Either that,
or he's an insane killer.

277
00:16:17,104 --> 00:16:18,397
I'd keep an eye on him.

278
00:16:20,232 --> 00:16:21,275
Will do.

279
00:16:27,156 --> 00:16:28,741
Did you find anything
in his background?

280
00:16:29,033 --> 00:16:30,075
Clean criminal record.

281
00:16:30,451 --> 00:16:31,494
He's Austin-born and raised

282
00:16:31,619 --> 00:16:34,830
former used-bookstore clerk.
Currently unemployed.

283
00:16:35,164 --> 00:16:37,082
Does he have an alibi
for the night of the murders?

284
00:16:37,208 --> 00:16:38,417
Wylie checked. No alibi.

285
00:16:39,001 --> 00:16:41,378
Well... if he isn't our killer

286
00:16:42,505 --> 00:16:43,756
maybe he's plugged
into the murders

287
00:16:43,881 --> 00:16:45,382
in a way
we don't understand yet.

288
00:16:45,549 --> 00:16:48,427
- We should put a tail on him.
- Yeah, you do that.

289
00:16:50,095 --> 00:16:52,056
Uh, one more thing.

290
00:16:53,891 --> 00:16:56,685
Ranger Ayres told me about your
encounter with the poachers.

291
00:17:02,233 --> 00:17:03,901
- Okay.
- Well, she said that

292
00:17:04,026 --> 00:17:06,862
you came on a little strong
with one of 'em.

293
00:17:07,571 --> 00:17:10,241
- Is that what happened?
- He caught me by surprise.

294
00:17:10,991 --> 00:17:12,117
I was a little aggressive
in the moment.

295
00:17:12,243 --> 00:17:13,369
It won't happen again.

296
00:17:14,328 --> 00:17:16,413
- Is there anything else goin' on?
- Like what?

297
00:17:17,081 --> 00:17:18,123
Well...

298
00:17:19,750 --> 00:17:21,794
We're all still feeling
Vega's death.

299
00:17:22,586 --> 00:17:23,629
I know I am.

300
00:17:25,464 --> 00:17:27,049
Did the Army assign you
a counselor

301
00:17:27,174 --> 00:17:29,176
- when you left Special Forces?
- They did.

302
00:17:30,344 --> 00:17:32,263
Might be time to get in touch
with him again.

303
00:17:33,305 --> 00:17:34,682
It's good to talk to someone.

304
00:17:36,016 --> 00:17:37,059
It's helping me.

305
00:17:37,268 --> 00:17:38,853
I'll think about it.
Anything else?

306
00:17:39,562 --> 00:17:40,688
Nope, that's it.

307
00:17:47,152 --> 00:17:48,195
Hey.

308
00:17:49,655 --> 00:17:50,698
Thanks.

309
00:17:52,658 --> 00:17:53,701
No problem.

310
00:18:07,756 --> 00:18:08,799
Cho?

311
00:18:09,675 --> 00:18:12,052
- Cho?
- Yeah?

312
00:18:13,429 --> 00:18:14,471
Can I come with you?

313
00:18:17,683 --> 00:18:19,393
It's just that I, I know
you're shorthanded

314
00:18:19,518 --> 00:18:21,687
and I thought
maybe I could be useful.

315
00:18:24,148 --> 00:18:25,482
When was the last time
you shot your weapon?

316
00:18:25,608 --> 00:18:27,651
Couple days ago.
I stay current.

317
00:18:29,778 --> 00:18:30,821
All right.

318
00:18:33,866 --> 00:18:36,160
Get some dinner.
Be ready in an hour.

319
00:18:36,368 --> 00:18:37,411
Okay.

320
00:18:48,547 --> 00:18:50,799
Closing time.
I'm kicking you out.

321
00:18:51,133 --> 00:18:52,927
Oh, come on,
I have a free game here.

322
00:18:53,886 --> 00:18:55,471
Okay, tell you what.

323
00:18:56,388 --> 00:19:00,017
You bring me that case of beer
and put it over there

324
00:19:00,351 --> 00:19:01,769
and I'll let you play
your free game.

325
00:19:02,811 --> 00:19:03,854
You got it.

326
00:19:05,397 --> 00:19:07,566
My pleasure, Angela?

327
00:19:08,275 --> 00:19:09,360
Amy?

328
00:19:10,694 --> 00:19:11,737
Arlene?

329
00:19:11,862 --> 00:19:13,864
How do you know my name
starts with an "A"?

330
00:19:13,989 --> 00:19:16,200
'Cause a person
with the initials APJ

331
00:19:16,325 --> 00:19:18,911
has all the high scores
on that machine over there

332
00:19:19,161 --> 00:19:21,747
Somethin' to pass the time
on those quiet nights.

333
00:19:21,914 --> 00:19:22,957
Yep.

334
00:19:23,082 --> 00:19:25,000
APJ likes to play pinball

335
00:19:25,125 --> 00:19:27,252
instead of wiping down
the beer cooler.

336
00:19:27,670 --> 00:19:29,004
That's a very clever trick.

337
00:19:30,047 --> 00:19:31,799
Well, it's not rocket surgery.

338
00:19:33,092 --> 00:19:35,177
Looks like you have
three free games.

339
00:19:35,344 --> 00:19:38,138
Three, that's what I'm talkin' about.

340
00:19:38,305 --> 00:19:41,308
He thinks he's gonna impress me
with "three."

341
00:19:42,685 --> 00:19:43,852
How's that, now?

342
00:19:44,436 --> 00:19:46,397
Well, three's meaningful to you.

343
00:19:46,730 --> 00:19:49,108
Yeah. It is.
How'd you know?

344
00:19:49,233 --> 00:19:52,069
Mm, well, because three
is meaningful to everyone.

345
00:19:52,194 --> 00:19:56,240
I say three and you're impressed
because you have three kids.

346
00:19:56,365 --> 00:19:58,909
Wait, now. How do you know
I have three kids?

347
00:19:59,034 --> 00:20:01,120
I don't.
I, I was just guessing.

348
00:20:01,245 --> 00:20:03,998
That's what I mean. I...
I'm gonna...

349
00:20:04,248 --> 00:20:06,000
Don't worry 'bout that.
I'm gonna settle up my account.

350
00:20:06,125 --> 00:20:08,419
- How much do I owe you?
- You paid already.

351
00:20:08,585 --> 00:20:10,212
- Did I leave you a tip?
- Yep.

352
00:20:10,337 --> 00:20:12,131
- Was it a good tip?
- Yeah.

353
00:20:12,631 --> 00:20:14,049
- Well, that's nice.
- Mm-hm.

354
00:20:14,925 --> 00:20:17,094
Mm, hey, whoa. Okay.

355
00:20:18,595 --> 00:20:21,098
Just sleep it off on the couch
in the back.

356
00:20:21,348 --> 00:20:22,808
Keys'll be there in the morning.

357
00:20:22,975 --> 00:20:24,184
Coffee and aspirin, too.

358
00:20:24,685 --> 00:20:27,438
Well, that's a very generous
offer, Adriana, thank you.

359
00:20:27,563 --> 00:20:29,565
- Mm-mm.
- Nope, okay.

360
00:20:30,149 --> 00:20:31,275
But I think
I'm gonna walk it off.

361
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:33,986
- I need to clear my head.
- Suit yourself.

362
00:20:34,528 --> 00:20:37,823
Thank you.
Thank you very much.

363
00:20:38,157 --> 00:20:39,199
Amber!

364
00:20:39,950 --> 00:20:41,952
Are you sure
you're not psychic?

365
00:20:42,286 --> 00:20:44,997
That is the one thing
I am very sure I am not.

366
00:20:45,247 --> 00:20:46,415
- Hm.
- 'Night!

367
00:20:46,540 --> 00:20:47,666
Good night.

368
00:21:32,427 --> 00:21:33,470
I feel like this is a job

369
00:21:33,595 --> 00:21:35,764
that'll be replaced
by robots someday.

370
00:21:37,265 --> 00:21:38,475
Someday soon.

371
00:21:40,519 --> 00:21:42,562
This is being in the field.
It's not all action.

372
00:21:43,146 --> 00:21:44,189
Right.

373
00:21:56,535 --> 00:21:57,577
Is this any good?

374
00:22:00,205 --> 00:22:01,248
It's Dostoevsky.

375
00:22:03,250 --> 00:22:04,292
Is that good or bad?

376
00:22:07,712 --> 00:22:08,755
Okay.

377
00:22:28,150 --> 00:22:29,192
Morning.

378
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:38,702
Oh, come on.

379
00:23:01,266 --> 00:23:02,309
Who's that?

380
00:23:04,936 --> 00:23:06,605
Neighbor. Five doors down.

381
00:23:07,814 --> 00:23:10,025
- What are they doing?
- Talking.

382
00:23:10,233 --> 00:23:11,401
- Should we write that down?
- No.

383
00:23:14,779 --> 00:23:18,116
So, I bet Vega was pretty good
at all this stuff, right?

384
00:23:22,579 --> 00:23:25,665
- Yeah, she was.
- Thought so.

385
00:23:28,376 --> 00:23:29,419
Hey.

386
00:23:30,837 --> 00:23:32,672
If you wanna be out here,
I can show you the ropes.

387
00:23:32,797 --> 00:23:35,258
But do it because you want to,
not because you miss her, okay?

388
00:23:37,469 --> 00:23:39,346
I'm just tired
of being back in the office

389
00:23:39,471 --> 00:23:40,597
when you could use me
out here.

390
00:23:42,224 --> 00:23:44,059
- I'm ready.
- Okay.

391
00:23:48,438 --> 00:23:49,648
Stay here,
watch the house.

392
00:23:55,946 --> 00:23:56,988
Excuse me, ma'am?

393
00:23:58,198 --> 00:23:59,366
I'm Agent Cho, FBI.

394
00:23:59,741 --> 00:24:01,159
Whoa, okay,
what's going on?

395
00:24:01,910 --> 00:24:04,120
I have a few questions about
your neighbor, Gabriel Osbourne?

396
00:24:04,913 --> 00:24:05,956
Oh.

397
00:24:06,081 --> 00:24:07,123
What were you talking about?

398
00:24:08,833 --> 00:24:10,502
- Nothing.
- You sat there for three minutes

399
00:24:10,627 --> 00:24:11,670
talking about nothing?

400
00:24:14,548 --> 00:24:16,591
I asked him
if I was gonna find love.

401
00:24:17,259 --> 00:24:18,969
- I have a date tonight.
- You go to Gabriel often?

402
00:24:19,427 --> 00:24:21,846
I know how it sounds.
It's crazy, I know.

403
00:24:22,305 --> 00:24:23,682
But I used to date this guy

404
00:24:23,807 --> 00:24:25,016
and Gabriel told me
he was married

405
00:24:25,141 --> 00:24:26,726
and he had never met him,
he just knew.

406
00:24:27,227 --> 00:24:28,311
I don't believe in psychics.

407
00:24:29,854 --> 00:24:31,106
But I believe in Gabriel.

408
00:24:46,288 --> 00:24:47,330
Cho!

409
00:24:49,207 --> 00:24:50,250
Gabriel!

410
00:24:52,711 --> 00:24:54,004
Gabriel, hang tight.
It's gonna be okay.

411
00:24:54,421 --> 00:24:55,589
- What happened?
- I don't... I don't know.

412
00:24:55,797 --> 00:24:57,591
- He just collapsed.
- I'll call an ambulance.

413
00:24:59,259 --> 00:25:00,635
Gabriel... Gabriel!

414
00:25:01,970 --> 00:25:03,096
- You.
- Yeah?

415
00:25:04,347 --> 00:25:05,390
She says she's okay.

416
00:25:06,182 --> 00:25:08,310
She says...
She says she's okay.

417
00:25:08,643 --> 00:25:09,686
Who are you talking about?

418
00:25:11,146 --> 00:25:13,732
The pain is all gone, okay?

419
00:25:13,982 --> 00:25:16,192
She says she's okay.
You don't gotta be sad anymore.

420
00:25:18,403 --> 00:25:19,446
Are you talking about Michelle?

421
00:25:19,904 --> 00:25:21,823
- What's going on?
- What?

422
00:25:23,408 --> 00:25:24,451
It's red clay.

423
00:25:26,077 --> 00:25:28,246
It's white bones,
and they're wrapped in red clay.

424
00:26:00,528 --> 00:26:02,113
Did you get an update
from the hospital

425
00:26:02,238 --> 00:26:03,281
on Gabriel's condition?

426
00:26:03,406 --> 00:26:05,700
He refused to go to the hospital.
He doesn't trust doctors.

427
00:26:05,825 --> 00:26:08,495
- He needs to see a doctor.
- Yeah. We tried.

428
00:26:09,120 --> 00:26:10,163
You workin' on a new lead?

429
00:26:10,955 --> 00:26:13,041
This is where Donnie Putnam
and Megan Brooks were killed.

430
00:26:13,166 --> 00:26:15,293
But this area is interesting.

431
00:26:15,543 --> 00:26:16,586
What about it?

432
00:26:16,961 --> 00:26:19,839
This area here is known
for its red clay deposits.

433
00:26:19,964 --> 00:26:21,508
It's less than a mile
from the murder scene.

434
00:26:21,716 --> 00:26:23,802
- Okay.
- Gabriel said something.

435
00:26:23,927 --> 00:26:26,262
He had a, a, a vision
after his seizure.

436
00:26:26,388 --> 00:26:28,598
He said something
about white bones in red Clay.

437
00:26:29,140 --> 00:26:32,102
Wylie... You know Gabriel's
not a real psychic.

438
00:26:33,687 --> 00:26:35,313
I think we should look
into this area.

439
00:26:35,689 --> 00:26:37,399
We can't go
on a wild-goose chase

440
00:26:37,524 --> 00:26:38,900
because of something
Gabriel said.

441
00:26:42,112 --> 00:26:43,154
- You okay?
- Yeah.

442
00:26:43,655 --> 00:26:45,782
- You sure?
- Yeah. Yeah, I'm fine.

443
00:26:46,408 --> 00:26:48,702
This isn't about Vega, okay?
This is about a real lead.

444
00:26:49,703 --> 00:26:50,870
It wouldn't hurt to look,
would it?

445
00:26:51,746 --> 00:26:52,789
All right.

446
00:26:53,373 --> 00:26:54,416
We'll look into it.

447
00:26:59,462 --> 00:27:02,173
- So, what do you think?
- Eh, ground's tough.

448
00:27:02,674 --> 00:27:04,008
Don't know what you expect
to find here.

449
00:27:04,843 --> 00:27:07,554
It's a shot in the dark
but can't hurt to take a look.

450
00:27:08,388 --> 00:27:09,973
We'll go up and back,
up and back

451
00:27:10,098 --> 00:27:11,141
'til we cover the area.

452
00:27:11,307 --> 00:27:13,268
If Nicky smells something
worth checking out

453
00:27:13,393 --> 00:27:14,519
he'll bark twice like this.

454
00:27:15,937 --> 00:27:16,980
Okay, thanks.

455
00:27:18,815 --> 00:27:19,858
What did Gabriel say to you?

456
00:27:20,567 --> 00:27:23,027
He said, "white bones
wrapped in red clay."

457
00:27:23,153 --> 00:27:24,529
I know that. What else?

458
00:27:24,654 --> 00:27:26,197
And what did he say
to make you believe in him?

459
00:27:28,616 --> 00:27:30,952
- He said she's okay.
- Who?

460
00:27:31,411 --> 00:27:32,620
Michelle. She's okay.

461
00:27:33,997 --> 00:27:36,040
Wherever she is
she's okay.

462
00:27:36,916 --> 00:27:38,084
And he knew
where she was shot.

463
00:27:38,376 --> 00:27:40,670
Vega's death was on the news.
It's no secret.

464
00:27:40,920 --> 00:27:41,963
It didn't feel like that.

465
00:27:42,464 --> 00:27:45,508
- He's not a real psychic, Wylie.
- You can't know that.

466
00:27:46,009 --> 00:27:47,177
You can't know that for sure.

467
00:27:56,436 --> 00:27:58,772
Jane, I'm glad
I could find you.

468
00:27:59,564 --> 00:28:01,399
Well, I'm trying to be
more findable these days.

469
00:28:01,649 --> 00:28:04,194
"You know. Look, we're running
a ghost ship right now."

470
00:28:04,778 --> 00:28:06,780
We need you.
Are you ready to come in?

471
00:28:07,322 --> 00:28:09,282
Uh, yeah,
I think I can do that.

472
00:28:10,575 --> 00:28:11,618
Are you nearby?

473
00:28:12,035 --> 00:28:15,872
Well, to be honest,
I have no idea where I am.

474
00:28:36,100 --> 00:28:37,477
I know I missed your call
last night.

475
00:28:37,602 --> 00:28:39,312
I, I, I didn't...
I didn't mean to.

476
00:28:40,647 --> 00:28:41,689
I'm sorry.

477
00:28:42,398 --> 00:28:44,192
- What are you doin' here?
- I'm back.

478
00:28:45,401 --> 00:28:47,362
What does that mean exactly:
"You're back"?

479
00:28:48,196 --> 00:28:50,448
Well, it means
I'm figuring stuff out.

480
00:28:50,573 --> 00:28:52,951
I'm, I'm figuring it out.

481
00:28:54,869 --> 00:28:55,912
It's good to you see you.

482
00:28:57,997 --> 00:28:59,040
It's good to see you, too.

483
00:29:01,209 --> 00:29:02,252
So, what's goin' on here?

484
00:29:02,919 --> 00:29:04,629
You came just in time.
Come on.

485
00:29:05,755 --> 00:29:06,798
So I see.

486
00:29:19,060 --> 00:29:20,395
We're lookin'
for a serial killer.

487
00:29:25,706 --> 00:29:28,125
Five victims, all killed
using the same gun

488
00:29:28,250 --> 00:29:30,836
that killed Donnie Putnam
and Megan Brooks.

489
00:29:31,879 --> 00:29:33,130
They were all killed
in the past year.

490
00:29:33,755 --> 00:29:35,215
They all had
their fingernails removed.

491
00:29:35,883 --> 00:29:37,050
So we're looking
for a serial killer.

492
00:29:37,968 --> 00:29:40,179
The first three victims
had no IDs on them.

493
00:29:40,304 --> 00:29:42,389
That and the way they were
dressed leads me to believe

494
00:29:42,514 --> 00:29:44,683
that they were either homeless
or drifters.

495
00:29:44,892 --> 00:29:47,519
Victims four and five
were foreign-exchange students

496
00:29:47,644 --> 00:29:49,271
that were reported missing
two months ago.

497
00:29:49,897 --> 00:29:52,357
Add Megan and Donnie it brings the total
number of victims to seven.

498
00:29:53,192 --> 00:29:55,194
We'll consult with
the profilers at Quantico.

499
00:29:55,444 --> 00:29:56,487
Help expand the search

500
00:29:56,612 --> 00:29:59,031
and see if there's any other
consistent patterns

501
00:29:59,156 --> 00:30:00,199
with the other victims.

502
00:30:00,324 --> 00:30:02,034
- What about the media?
- Eh, we'll sit on it.

503
00:30:02,618 --> 00:30:04,203
Gabriel Osbourne took us
to a field

504
00:30:04,328 --> 00:30:05,871
that had five bodies
buried in it.

505
00:30:06,288 --> 00:30:08,916
If he didn't do it,
he knows who did.

506
00:30:09,333 --> 00:30:10,375
All right, I'll bring him in.

507
00:30:16,507 --> 00:30:18,592
Now, he won't ever admit it,
but he's in pain.

508
00:30:19,968 --> 00:30:21,553
It's like you met him.

509
00:30:26,099 --> 00:30:27,184
Not here just to talk.

510
00:30:29,186 --> 00:30:31,188
- I'm gonna go with you?
- That's right.

511
00:30:32,439 --> 00:30:34,650
- Are you arresting me?
- If that's how you want it.

512
00:30:38,111 --> 00:30:40,531
Gabriel, is everything all right?

513
00:30:42,449 --> 00:30:43,492
Call my sister.

514
00:30:52,251 --> 00:30:54,419
Hey. Heard you had a spell.

515
00:30:55,045 --> 00:30:56,088
How are you feeling now?

516
00:30:57,464 --> 00:30:58,507
Fine.

517
00:30:58,966 --> 00:31:00,008
Get tired but I'm okay.

518
00:31:02,594 --> 00:31:04,596
Something different about you
from the last time we talked.

519
00:31:05,639 --> 00:31:06,682
You look lighter.

520
00:31:07,933 --> 00:31:08,976
Less conflicted.

521
00:31:11,562 --> 00:31:13,689
Number three, you saw it
and found an answer, huh?

522
00:31:14,439 --> 00:31:17,818
The number three is incredibly
common, Gabriel.

523
00:31:18,986 --> 00:31:20,028
We see it everywhere.

524
00:31:20,195 --> 00:31:22,072
Red clay, little rarer.

525
00:31:22,531 --> 00:31:24,825
But, uh, not much.

526
00:31:31,415 --> 00:31:33,959
- I didn't wanna be right.
- Of course you did.

527
00:31:35,586 --> 00:31:37,129
I don't wanna see
these things.

528
00:31:37,879 --> 00:31:39,256
Okay, I don't ask
for these visions.

529
00:31:39,464 --> 00:31:40,882
Yeah, visions are a real drag.

530
00:31:41,675 --> 00:31:42,718
I know how you feel.

531
00:31:43,468 --> 00:31:44,761
You can't know how I feel.

532
00:31:46,138 --> 00:31:47,931
Yeah, I used to be you, Gabriel.

533
00:31:50,017 --> 00:31:51,101
What is that supposed to mean?

534
00:31:51,226 --> 00:31:53,854
You spent a year of your childhood
struggling with an illness.

535
00:31:54,563 --> 00:31:56,189
That's when you learned
to love to read.

536
00:31:56,523 --> 00:31:57,566
You used to play piano

537
00:31:57,691 --> 00:31:59,109
but you didn't like it,
so you quit.

538
00:32:00,485 --> 00:32:04,072
You're not half as unsure
of yourself as you pretend to be.

539
00:32:05,490 --> 00:32:06,533
Who told you all that?

540
00:32:07,576 --> 00:32:09,911
- My sister?
- Nobody. No one.

541
00:32:11,913 --> 00:32:12,956
You're lying.

542
00:32:14,750 --> 00:32:15,834
And you don't have visions.

543
00:32:16,293 --> 00:32:19,129
No, I don't have visions,
and neither do you, Gabriel.

544
00:32:21,840 --> 00:32:23,050
Why are you playing games
with me?

545
00:32:23,508 --> 00:32:26,720
I need you to know that
I understand your little tricks.

546
00:32:30,182 --> 00:32:31,224
I don't play tricks.

547
00:32:33,185 --> 00:32:35,062
You're the one who's playing
tricks with me right now.

548
00:32:36,271 --> 00:32:38,273
- I only wanna help.
- If you wanna help

549
00:32:38,940 --> 00:32:41,234
you can start by telling me
how you know what you know.

550
00:32:43,987 --> 00:32:47,074
I had another vision
you should know about.

551
00:32:49,159 --> 00:32:51,036
I saw that the killer
is going to kill again.

552
00:32:52,329 --> 00:32:53,372
Tonight.

553
00:32:54,706 --> 00:32:57,250
And if you won't listen to me,
I'll tell everyone.

554
00:32:58,835 --> 00:33:00,879
- Okay, I have to warn people.
- You can't leave.

555
00:33:01,421 --> 00:33:03,548
- Why not?
- Because I came in here

556
00:33:03,674 --> 00:33:05,467
to figure out
if you are just a fraud

557
00:33:06,551 --> 00:33:07,803
or if you are a monster.

558
00:33:12,641 --> 00:33:13,684
What did you decide?

559
00:33:15,310 --> 00:33:16,687
You have to stay here, Gabriel.

560
00:33:23,360 --> 00:33:24,695
We didn't find anything
at Gabriel's house.

561
00:33:25,320 --> 00:33:26,363
Well, he's not breaking.

562
00:33:26,863 --> 00:33:29,366
- He won't admit he's a fraud?
- Well, he's not a fraud.

563
00:33:29,741 --> 00:33:30,784
Are you saying
he's really psychic?

564
00:33:30,992 --> 00:33:32,494
- No.
- Then what is he?

565
00:33:34,329 --> 00:33:36,289
I don't know. I don't...
We have to keep him here.

566
00:33:36,873 --> 00:33:37,916
All right.

567
00:33:44,589 --> 00:33:45,882
Excuse me, can I help you?

568
00:33:46,174 --> 00:33:48,260
Where's my brother?
Do you have my brother?

569
00:33:48,385 --> 00:33:49,678
I am Gabriel Osbourne's attorney.

570
00:33:49,928 --> 00:33:50,971
I've come to secure his release

571
00:33:51,096 --> 00:33:52,597
from the illegal arrest
you've placed him under.

572
00:33:53,765 --> 00:33:55,976
Well, we only brought him in
for questioning.

573
00:33:56,184 --> 00:33:58,478
I have a writ of habeas corpus
being couriered to Judge Decker.

574
00:33:58,603 --> 00:34:01,148
Do I need to get him out of bed or are you
prepared to release Gabriel immediately?

575
00:34:05,902 --> 00:34:06,945
Mr. Osbourne!

576
00:34:07,487 --> 00:34:08,530
Give us a shot.

577
00:34:08,697 --> 00:34:09,740
- Mr. Osbourne.
- Mr. Osbourne!

578
00:34:09,865 --> 00:34:11,867
Mr. Osbourne,
I just have a few questions.

579
00:34:12,075 --> 00:34:13,118
- Mr. Osbourne!
- Gabriel!

580
00:34:13,243 --> 00:34:14,619
Ladies and gentlemen....

581
00:34:15,328 --> 00:34:16,872
Ladies and gentlemen,
thank you for coming.

582
00:34:17,789 --> 00:34:21,001
My client, Gabriel Osbourne has been
illegally detained by the FBI

583
00:34:21,126 --> 00:34:23,253
for attempting to help them
capture a serial killer

584
00:34:23,628 --> 00:34:25,964
A serial killer that is currently
on the loose in Austin.

585
00:34:26,465 --> 00:34:28,550
Mr. Osbourne, we just need
to know a few things.

586
00:34:28,675 --> 00:34:30,385
- Do you know any...
- Let's have Gabriel tell the story

587
00:34:30,510 --> 00:34:31,553
in his own words.

588
00:34:33,180 --> 00:34:37,434
I had a vision that helped them
find five bodies today.

589
00:34:37,976 --> 00:34:39,311
They don't have
any suspects.

590
00:34:39,728 --> 00:34:43,231
FBI thinks it was me.
They wanna frame me.

591
00:34:44,149 --> 00:34:45,233
They wanna hide the truth.

592
00:34:47,277 --> 00:34:49,279
There's a serial killer out there.

593
00:34:50,030 --> 00:34:53,617
He is a man with an evil heart
and an appetite to kill.

594
00:34:54,159 --> 00:34:55,243
He's not done killing.

595
00:34:56,703 --> 00:34:59,539
He won't stop,
and he, he can't stop.

596
00:34:59,664 --> 00:35:01,166
He's... He's gonna kill again.

597
00:35:01,917 --> 00:35:02,959
That's all for now.
Thank you.

598
00:35:03,084 --> 00:35:04,127
Stewart, Stewart, if we...

599
00:35:04,294 --> 00:35:05,337
We just have a few more questions.

600
00:35:05,462 --> 00:35:07,047
- "We wanna know more."
- This is going badly.

601
00:35:07,589 --> 00:35:09,716
- Mr. Osbourne!
- Yes, it is.

602
00:35:10,884 --> 00:35:12,803
But we're gonna stay focused
on finding the killer.

603
00:35:14,095 --> 00:35:15,138
I'll stay on Gabriel.

604
00:35:16,389 --> 00:35:17,432
You do that.

605
00:35:18,058 --> 00:35:19,684
I'm gonna feed myself
to the sharks.

606
00:35:26,024 --> 00:35:27,317
Great. Thanks for the update.

607
00:35:29,069 --> 00:35:30,111
What's the word from the office?

608
00:35:30,445 --> 00:35:31,488
Police lines are flooded.

609
00:35:31,655 --> 00:35:33,156
People are seeing
serial killers everywhere.

610
00:35:34,574 --> 00:35:35,826
And not a peep from these two.

611
00:35:41,581 --> 00:35:42,624
Who's that?

612
00:35:44,626 --> 00:35:45,669
What should we do?

613
00:35:46,253 --> 00:35:48,088
You stay put.
I'll call you if I need you.

614
00:36:03,937 --> 00:36:05,063
Stop, FBI!

615
00:36:07,858 --> 00:36:08,900
C'mon out.

616
00:36:12,612 --> 00:36:14,072
- You're the neighbor, right?
- Mm-hm.

617
00:36:14,447 --> 00:36:16,116
- Why'd you run?
- I was scared.

618
00:36:16,491 --> 00:36:18,535
Gabriel was on the news and said
there was a killer on the loose

619
00:36:18,660 --> 00:36:19,703
and then I saw you lurking.

620
00:36:19,828 --> 00:36:21,037
Okay, go on home.

621
00:36:34,632 --> 00:36:35,674
Wylie, hey.

622
00:36:38,552 --> 00:36:40,805
- What happened?
- I don't know. Somebody hit me.

623
00:36:41,555 --> 00:36:43,265
- You all right?
- Yeah.

624
00:36:44,183 --> 00:36:45,226
Come on, get up.

625
00:36:47,520 --> 00:36:49,063
- Going in, okay? All right.
- Okay.

626
00:37:16,382 --> 00:37:17,425
- Can I get a second?
- Yeah.

627
00:37:18,884 --> 00:37:19,927
How you holdin' up?

628
00:37:20,594 --> 00:37:21,637
I don't know.

629
00:37:23,389 --> 00:37:25,307
I don't think I'm cut out
for the field.

630
00:37:26,934 --> 00:37:27,977
This is rough work.

631
00:37:28,102 --> 00:37:29,228
You're gonna get banged up
every once in a while.

632
00:37:30,980 --> 00:37:32,189
I don't think I can do this.

633
00:37:33,441 --> 00:37:34,984
You wanna go back to the office
and answer phones?

634
00:37:35,234 --> 00:37:36,777
"Okay these guys..."

635
00:37:37,778 --> 00:37:38,821
"That's correct."

636
00:37:41,282 --> 00:37:42,324
No.

637
00:37:43,451 --> 00:37:44,827
I wanna stay.
What can I do, here?

638
00:37:45,494 --> 00:37:47,246
We need to put together
a description of your attacker.

639
00:37:48,330 --> 00:37:50,374
I don't know if it was Gabriel
or someone else who attacked me

640
00:37:50,499 --> 00:37:51,542
and now Gabriel's gone.

641
00:37:52,126 --> 00:37:53,627
And Jane's inside.
Go see him.

642
00:37:54,753 --> 00:37:55,796
- Why?
- Just go.

643
00:38:05,222 --> 00:38:07,683
Hey. How you feelin'?

644
00:38:09,059 --> 00:38:10,436
They wanna check me out
at the hospital

645
00:38:10,561 --> 00:38:11,979
but Cho said
to see you first.

646
00:38:12,146 --> 00:38:14,565
Hm. Yeah, what do you remember
about the person who attacked you?

647
00:38:16,108 --> 00:38:17,318
Nothing. I didn't see the guy.

648
00:38:18,402 --> 00:38:20,529
Oh, you know more
than you think you do.

649
00:38:21,113 --> 00:38:22,156
I just want you
to close your eyes.

650
00:38:23,657 --> 00:38:24,700
Okay, big breath in.

651
00:38:26,368 --> 00:38:27,411
And out.

652
00:38:28,662 --> 00:38:31,123
Good. One more...Breath.

653
00:38:33,083 --> 00:38:34,126
And out.

654
00:38:37,463 --> 00:38:40,174
Now, I want you to listen
very carefully to my voice.

655
00:38:42,092 --> 00:38:45,221
You hear no other sound
other than my voice.

656
00:38:47,890 --> 00:38:49,350
There's someone behind you.

657
00:38:50,893 --> 00:38:52,269
You don't know who it is.

658
00:38:54,438 --> 00:38:56,982
But you see something out
of the corner of your eye.

659
00:38:59,568 --> 00:39:01,779
No. No, I don't see anything.

660
00:39:02,446 --> 00:39:04,782
That's okay.
You're doing fine.

661
00:39:06,450 --> 00:39:07,576
You're doing fine.

662
00:39:09,828 --> 00:39:11,330
Right before you were hit

663
00:39:13,165 --> 00:39:14,875
there was a scent in the air

664
00:39:16,919 --> 00:39:18,671
A faint scent.

665
00:39:20,548 --> 00:39:22,383
Mm. Yeah.

666
00:39:24,843 --> 00:39:25,886
What was it?

667
00:39:29,390 --> 00:39:30,432
I don't know.

668
00:39:32,017 --> 00:39:33,352
Does it remind you of anything?

669
00:39:35,688 --> 00:39:37,314
My Uncle's fishing shed.

670
00:39:38,440 --> 00:39:40,109
Ah. Was it fish?

671
00:39:41,735 --> 00:39:44,154
No. He doesn't actually fish there.

672
00:39:46,407 --> 00:39:47,533
He just went there
to drink.

673
00:39:48,284 --> 00:39:49,827
- What did he drink?
- Beer.

674
00:39:51,745 --> 00:39:53,205
It smells like old, spilled beer.

675
00:39:55,791 --> 00:39:57,585
- You did very well.
- Thanks.

676
00:40:01,422 --> 00:40:02,548
Okay, I got it. Thanks.

677
00:40:02,798 --> 00:40:05,050
Mustang Creek Brewery.
It shut down around a year ago.

678
00:40:05,175 --> 00:40:06,802
It's only a mile from where
the bodies were found.

679
00:40:06,927 --> 00:40:07,970
Let's go.

680
00:40:25,112 --> 00:40:26,447
Get a perimeter set up,
three-block radius.

681
00:40:26,572 --> 00:40:27,615
I got the front.

